# Widget Factory

[![CI](
  https://github.com/example/widget/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg
)](https://github.com/example/widget/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
[![License: MIT](
  https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg
)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)

Widget Factory builds widgets. It is fast, small, and has no runtime
dependencies, which makes it a good fit for embedded targets and
command-line tools alike.

## Install

```sh
cargo install widget-factory
```

## Usage

- `widget new <name>` creates a widget.
- `widget build` compiles every widget in the current directory and
  writes the results to `target/widgets`.
    - Pass `--release` for optimised output.
- `widget clean`

| Command | Description                        |
| ------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `new`   | Create a widget                    |
| `build` | Build all widgets in the workspace |
| `clean` | Remove build output                |

1) First, read the [contributing guide](CONTRIBUTING.md).
2) Then open an issue describing the change you want to make before
   sending a pull request.

> **Note** Widgets are not gadgets.

